Question: The ground level of $\mathrm{Cl}$ is ${ }^2 \mathrm{P}_{3 / 2}$ and a ${ }^2 \mathrm{P}_{1 / 2}$ level lies $881 \mathrm{~cm}^{-1}$ above it. Calculate the electronic contribution to the molar Gibbs energy of $\mathrm{Cl}$ atoms at  $500 \mathrm{~K}$.

Options:
A. -8.57 $\mathrm{~kJ} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$
B. -4.12 kJ mol^{-1}
C. -5.27 $\mathrm{~kJ} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$
D. -6.42 $\mathrm{~kJ} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$
E. -9.81 kJ mol^{-1}
F. -10.26 kJ mol^{-1}
G. -11.34 kJ mol^{-1}
H. -2.95 kJ mol^{-1}
I. -3.58 kJ mol^{-1}
J. -7.35 $\mathrm{~kJ} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$

Choose the best answer. In the JSON answer field, return only one option letter.
